  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "MUNIT truncates dimension toward zero, lifts over array inputs, and returns #NAME? in compatibility version 1",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, MUNIT(dimension) truncates dimension toward zero, rejects values below 1 (or above 1,048,576) with #VALUE!, and lifts over array inputs (returning per-element top-left scalars such as #VALUE! beside 1 for MUNIT({0,2})). Under compatibility version 1, @MUNIT evaluates to #NAME? (_xludf.MUNIT).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in fn2_questions (fn2_q066, fn2_q068, fn2_q166) and prefix_metadata (row 158), and matched across 1,277/1,277 full-bank MUNIT rows.",
